6.194.m:
In the Kali age, however, she met with decline, afflicted by the disease of heresy;
by your command she went quickly back to Vaikuṇṭha;
[yet] as soon as she is remembered by you, Liberation comes even today in haste.

6.197.m:
Occupied in every direction by gopīs, adorned with calves, of wondrous form and great splendor, / the glorious Gokula shines;

in its center, the radiant, exalted mansion of Hari shines brightly, / in which the mistress of Nanda’s household, and those who are praised with Rādhā, rejoiced;

the great fortune that is always contemplated within by Umā’s lord and other [gods] / shines through the sweet-formed son of that [mother], with rays that illuminate the multitude of eggs [of the universe].
